    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F28471DFA0F4183976163E181A695BE1/jobs/468439": {
      "title": "Equipment Operator Groundsperson (80025)",
      "description": "Equipment Operator Groundsperson (80025) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Equipment Operator Groundsperson (80025) New Rochelle - New Rochelle, NY 10801 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.00 - $23.00 Hourly Position Type Full Time Apply Description Duties and Responsibilities Daily cleanup and maintenance of the campus grounds including but not limited to: Mow lawns, rake leaves, shovel snow, repair concrete and paved areas, hedge shrubs, prune trees or remove if necessary, install and repair sprinkler systems, plant flowers, install landscaping, golf turf maintenance, dig trenches, fertilizing and pest management, maintain a clean shop, minor vehicle and equipment repairs, help with off-loading deliveries, moving heavy objects, dumpster control, fence installations and repair, storm drain maintenance, Christmas decorating and any other duties deemed necessary. Qualifications Required Experience High school diploma At least one year in a grounds related field Must be able to lift 100lbs and do daily physical labor Heavy equipment operation and ability to work with power tools Valid Driver’s License Required Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. About Iona/EEO Statement: Founded in 1940, Iona University is a private, Catholic, coeducational institution of learning in the tradition of the Edmund Rice Christian Brothers. Iona is a growing, highly accredited institution located just 20 miles north of Midtown Manhattan, with campuses in New Rochelle, Bronxville, and a new location in County Mayo, Ireland. With over 4,000 students, Iona offers small classes, engaged faculty, and a wide range of programs across the School of Arts & Science, the LaPenta School of Business (AACSB‑accredited), the NewYork‑Presbyterian Iona School of Nursing & Health Sciences, and the Hynes Institute for Entrepreneurship & Innovation. Recognized by The Princeton Review, The Wall Street Journal, Forbes, and U.S. News