    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F28471DFA0F4183976163E181A695BE1/jobs/503989": {
      "title": "Head Coach - Women's Varsity Flag Football (81648)",
      "description": "Head Coach - Women's Varsity Flag Football (81648) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Coach - Women's Varsity Flag Football (81648) Bronxville - Bronxville, NY 10708; New Rochelle - New Rochelle, NY 10801 Apply Overview Salary Range $65,000.00 - $65,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Apply Description Iona University, an NCAA Division I institution and member of the Metro Conference, seeks a highly motivated individual to serve as Head Coach for its inaugural Women’s Varsity Flag Football program. This is a full-time, 12-month position reporting to the Director of Athletics. The Head Coach will lead all aspects of program development, including recruiting and developing student-athletes, promoting academic success, managing staff and resources, supporting fundraising, and establishing a competitive, sustainable program aligned with Iona’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities Program Development and Timeline – Beginning in Fall 2026, establish the program’s foundation, including recruiting, infrastructure, scheduling, competition planning, and preparation for the inaugural season. The program is scheduled to begin varsity competition in Fall 2027. Training and Competition – Establish the program’s vision and competitive philosophy. Plan and conduct practices, training programs, game plans, strategies, and player-development initiatives. Develop a competitive schedule that supports student-athlete development and program growth. Recruiting – Beginning in Fall 2026, recruit qualified student-athletes who can succeed academically and athletically at Iona. Conduct all recruiting in accordance with applicable University, conference, NCAA, and governing-body rules and regulations. Representation and Program Promotion – Represent Iona professionally in interactions with officials, opponents, prospective student-athletes, families, media, alumni, donors, and the public. Promote the program and cultivate support from alumni, parents, donors, and other constituents. Budgeting and Fundraising – Participate in developing and managing the program budget within approved parameters. Collaborate with Athletics administration and University Advancement to establish and achieve fundraising goals. Compliance and Administration – Ensure compliance with institutional, conference, NCAA, and sport-specific rules and regulations, including those governing eligibility, recruiting, financial aid, scheduling, and academic progress. Work with Athletics Compliance to prepare and maintain required documentation. Student-Athlete Development and Academic Success – Foster an environment that prioritizes academic achievement, personal development, leadership, well-being, and the overall student-athlete experience. Collaborate with Athletics and University support services to promote success during and after students’ time at Iona. Staff Management – Recruit, hire, supervise, develop, and evaluate assistant coaches and other program staff as appropriate. Establish clear expectations and promote a positive, collaborative, and accountable team culture. Qualifications Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. About Iona/EEO Statement: Founded in 1940, Iona University is a private, Catholic, coeducational institution of learning in the tradition of the Edmund Rice Christian Brothers. Iona is a growing, highly accredited institution located just 20 miles north of Midtown Manhattan, with campuses in New Rochelle, Bronxville, and a new location in County Mayo, Ireland. With over 4,000 students, Iona offers small classes, engaged faculty, and a wide range of programs across the School of Arts & Science, the LaPenta School of Business (AACSB accredited), the NewYork Presbyterian Iona School of Nursing & Health Sciences, and the Hynes Institute for Entrepreneurship & Innovation. Recognized by The Princeton Review, The Wall Street Journal, Forbes, and U.S. News & World Report, Iona is nationally ranked for academic quality, social mobility, and long term return on investment. The University’s continued growth and rising reputation reflect its commitment to academic excellence, innovation, service, and opportunity. Iona University values and celebrates diversity and is committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive environment for all employees and applicants for employment. Iona is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will be considered free from discrimination based on any legally protected characteristic under applicable federal, state, or local laws. Iona University encourages applications from qualified candidates of all backgrounds. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
